# Every variable the code reads. All are optional and the defaults work for local development, so each is
# commented out: an empty value is not the same as unset (VITE_SHARE_ORIGIN= would blank the share origin).
# AI keys are not read from the environment: paste them in the app's AI provider dialog (kept in this browser's localStorage).

# --- App build (Vite reads these from .env.local at build time) ---

# Cloudflare Turnstile site key for share links; dev builds fall back to Cloudflare's always-pass test key.
# VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
# Origin of the share-link Worker (worker/); defaults to https://share.openflowkit.com.
# VITE_SHARE_ORIGIN=

# --- MCP server (set in the shell or the MCP client's env block, not in .env.local) ---

# Port of the local bridge the live editor connects to; defaults to 43119.
# OPENFLOWKIT_BRIDGE_PORT=
# Token the bridge requires on every request; unset means no token (requests are still origin-checked).
# OPENFLOWKIT_BRIDGE_TOKEN=
# HTTP transport (`npm --prefix mcp-server run start:http`): listen port, defaults to 8787.
# PORT=
# HTTP transport: bind address, defaults to 127.0.0.1 (localhost only).
# HOST=
# HTTP transport: comma-separated hostnames to answer when HOST is not localhost (required then).
# OPENFLOWKIT_ALLOWED_HOSTS=
# HTTP transport: app origin the viewer links to; defaults to the hosted app.
# APP_ORIGIN=

# --- Share Worker (worker/; Cloudflare settings, not .env) ---
# TURNSTILE_SECRET: `npx wrangler secret put TURNSTILE_SECRET` (see worker/README.md).
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS: optional Worker var, comma-separated app origins allowed by CORS (default https://app.openflowkit.com).
